\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Closes Stronger On Benign US CPI Data  \b0\par\par\uc2 354 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2006\par 21:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real closed stronger Wednesday on the release of benign U.S. inflation data.  \par \par \uc2 The real closed at BRL2.137 to the U.S. dollar, strengthening from Tuesday's close of BRL2.140.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. government early Wednesday announced the consumer price index rose by 0.4% in July, while core prices rose by only 0.2%, which was a relief after four straight 0.3% increases.  \par \par \uc2 The consumer inflation outlook is restrained, raising hopes that the U.S. Federal Reserve may extend the current pause in its monetary-tightening policy.  \par \par \uc2 That would be good news for the real as rising U.S. interest rates tend to attract investment away from emerging markets such as Brazil.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. decision canceled out the effect of news that \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to be increasing its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local market following large gains by the real Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced Wednesday that it will sound out market demand with a view to holding a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reverse swap auction.  \par \par \uc2 The auctions allow investors to swap paper linked to \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  variation for government paper linked to interest rates. The swap allows foreign investors to enjoy Brazil's high interest rates without \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure.  \par \par \uc2 If the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  detects interest in this kind of \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  during its survey later Wednesday, the bank will hold an auction Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The bank bought U.S. dollars at a snap auction Wednesday afternoon at a rate of BRL2.1335 reals to the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't reveal the volume of dollars purchased.  \par \par \uc2 Before the auction, at 1813 GMT, the real was trading at BRL2.133 to the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the spot auction weakened slightly toward its close at BRL2.137 per dollar  \par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began holding daily auctions to purchase dollars in October 2005 in an effort to rebuild the country's foreign reserves.  \par \par \uc2 -By Bernd Radowitz, Dow Jones Newswires; +55-21-3288 5004; bernd.radowitz@dowjones.com [ 16-08-06 1941GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1156 1843  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060816e28g000wt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
