\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's stocks fall; real slips on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 2006\par 17:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , July 20 (Reuters) - Brazilian stocks fell on Thursday on profit-taking after a rally the previous day and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by buying dollars and selling debt instruments.  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> finished 0.73 percent weaker at 2.193 per dollar after giving up all of Wednesday's gains. The real is still near its strongest level in five years.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $1.35 billion worth of so-called reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, rolling over a similar batch of paper maturing in August, in the first such auction since April.  \par \par \uc2 Joao Medeiros, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Pioneer brokerage, said the swap "works as if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was effectively buying dollars," and attributed the fall to the auction.  \par \par \uc2 The swaps, which allow investors to buy exposure to Brazil's lofty domestic interest rate without having to purchase the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , were originally sold to prevent the real from strengthening too much.  \par \par \uc2 Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  trimmed the key Selic interest rate by 0.5 percentage point to 20-year lows on Wednesday, as the market had been expecting, the rate of 14.75 percent is still high even for emerging markets.  \par \par \uc2 The bank also bought dollars on the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the 13th time in 14 sessions. Exporters have complained that the real's strength may hurt foreign sales.  \par \par \uc2 Wednesday's rally was triggered by U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke's suggestion that U.S. inflation is under control and U.S. interest rates may not rise as much as previously expected. That eased concerns that higher U.S. rates would reduce the attractiveness of Brazilian securities.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark Bovespa index at the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange <.BVSP> dropped 2.55 percent to 35,847 points after soaring 4.71 percent the previous day.  \par \par \uc2 Still, Alvaro Bandera, director of Agora Senior brokerage, said the market's general mood was positive after Bernanke's speech and Thursday's fall was mere profit-taking.  \par \par \uc2 "If there is a truce between Israel and Lebanon, things can get better a little more. We're still going to have volatility, but I'm working with a positive scenario," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, state oil company Petrobras -- the index's top heavyweight -- fell nearly 3 percent to 42.35 reais after its president, Jose Sergio Gabrielli, once again ruled out a fuel price hike while there is strong volatility on the world oil market. Petrobras last raised it gasoline and diesel prices in in September 2005.  \par \par \uc2 Shares in troubled airline Varig , which was sold for $24 million in an auction on Thursday, slumped 32.7 percent to 2.55 reais. Varig shares are not included in the Bovespa index but they traded actively on the eve of the auction, which was aimed to avoid the airline's bankruptcy.  \par \par \uc2 Shares of Perdigao , a food processing company, soared 4.4 percent to 28.6 reais on bets that rival Sadia would sweeten its recent takeover bid, rejected by Perdigao. Sadia shares ended practically flat at 6.1 reais. [20060720 153238 GMT]  \par \par \uc2 [20060720 214232 GMT]   \par \par \uc2 