\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's stocks fall on Petrobras, but real gains  \b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 2006\par 17:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Brazil, July 17 (Reuters) - Brazil's stocks fell on Monday, dragged down by plunging oil driller Petrobras, but the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained on heavy dollar inflows.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark Bovespa index at the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange <.BVSP> lost 1.37 percent to 34,886 points while the real <BRBY> gained 0.41 percent to 2.205 per U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The real strengthened despite tension in the Middle East and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars on the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the 10th time in 11 sessions it has moved to build up foreign reserves.  \par \par \uc2 State-run Petrobras fell 4.39 percent to 42.30 reais. The shares fell as investors battled over futures options that matured on Petrobras, the heaviest-weighted stock in the Bovespa index, said Luiz Roberto Monteiro, an investment analyst at Souza Barros brokerage in Sao Paulo.  \par \par \uc2 He said holders of Petrobras options at 44 reais had contributed to the decline by selling the stock, which closed Friday at 44.24 reais.  \par \par \uc2 Perdigao , Brazil's second largest meat processor, surged 17.61 percent to 27.05 reais after bigger rival Sadia made an unsolicited offer for a controlling stake in the company. Sadia shares gained 8.77 percent to 6.20 reais.  \par \par \uc2 Embraer , the world's fourth-largest commercial aircraft maker, lost 0.92 percent to 18.25 reais.  \par \par \uc2 The company said on Monday United Aviation, based in Kuwait, agreed to buy three Embraer executive jets: one Phenom 100, one Phenom 300, and one Legacy 600. The order would be valued at $33.1 million at list prices for the three aircraft.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060717e27h001ev\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
