\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  stocks gain but real slips on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 417 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2006\par 18:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , July 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stocks rose on Monday on optimism over increased dollar inflows from exports and diminishing expectations of U.S. interest rate rises.  \par \par \uc2 The national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained early but weakened after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for the first time since May, when market volatility curtailed purchases designed to build up foreign reserves.  \par \par \uc2 The Sao Paulo Stock Exchange's Bovespa index <.BVSP> finished 1.98 percent higher at 37,357 points. The real <BRBY> weakened 0.60 percent to 2.18 per U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "People weren't expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to return to the market," said Alexandre Vasarhelyi, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at ING in Sao Paulo.  \par \par \uc2 Brazil posted a better-than-expected $4.08 billion trade surplus in June, which helped increase the supply of dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and pushed the real higher. The country was expected to post a surplus of slightly more than $3 billion for the month, according to the median estimate of six international investment banks compiled by Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 Shares of Tim Participacoes , Brazil's second-largest wireless phone company, were among the biggest gainers in the Bovespa, surging 5.51 percent to 6.32 reais.  \par \par \uc2 The company said in a statement to the country's securities regulator that its controlling shareholder canceled a request to sell shares in Brazil and abroad, citing a "negative performance and growing volatility in capital markets."  \par \par \uc2 Investors sought shares of Tim Participacoes after selling the stock short ahead of the offering, said Tommy Taterka, a trader for brokerage Concordia.  \par \par \uc2 "The pressure to buy the stock is natural (after the sale cancellation)," Taterka said.  \par \par \uc2 State controlled oil company Petrobras , which is the heaviest-weighted stock in the benchmark Bovespa index, rose 0.97 percent to 43.60 reais.  \par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, the company unveiled a much larger investment budget for the next several years and on Monday it denied a newspaper report that it was planning to purchase a large stake in oil giant Rosneft as part of the Russian company's $11 billion share sale in July.  \par \par \uc2 Iron ore company CVRD rose 2.38 percent to 45.13 reais. CVRD said it bought the 45.5 percent stake it did not already own in aluminum smelter Valesul Aluminio SA from BHP Billiton Ltd./Plc for $27.5 million.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|U|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060703e273001ih\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
