\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil stocks,  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  drop after hitting records  \b0\par\par\uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2006\par 17:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Brazil, May 12 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stocks slumped on Friday as emerging market assets lost a bit of luster on rising yields for U.S. Treasuries and fears of higher U.S. inflation.  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> weakened some 2 percent to 2.144 per dollar after plunging nearly 2 percent in the previous session -- its biggest one-day loss in six months.  \par \par \uc2 It was also pressured as \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept up aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the spot market to build foreign reserves and please exporters by weakening the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Still, the real remains near its strongest five-year intraday level of 2.053 per dollar, which was hit on Wednesday before the Federal Reserve raised interest rates by a quarter-percentage point and left the door open to more increases, which could lure capital away from emerging markets.  \par \par \uc2 At the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange, the Bovespa <.BVSP> index fell 1.7 percent to 40,154 points after setting an all-time intraday high on Thursday before losing ground.  \par \par \uc2 "I'd say 90 percent of the selling is because of external factors," said Marcelo Voss, chief economist at the Novacao brokerage in Sao Paulo.  \par \par \uc2 Emerging market government bond yield spreads over U.S. Treasuries -- perceived as a gauge of risk -- widened 7 basis points to 187 basis points, according to the benchmark JP Morgan EMBI Plus Emerging Market Bond Index <11EMJ>.  \par \par \uc2 The Brazil spreads, closely watched by domestic financial markets, widened even more as U.S. Treasury yields rose following a spike in U.S. inflation expectations, as gauged by the University of Michigan.  \par \par \uc2 Brazil's financial markets have soared to a series of record highs over the last year, helped by improving economic fundamentals and a high benchmark interest rate, currently at 15.75 percent, which foreign investors find attractive.  \par \par \uc2 At the stock market, oil driller Petrobras , the heaviest weighted stock in the index, lost 0.93 percent to 46.92 reais. It is expected to post strong quarterly earnings after the market closes.  \par \par \uc2 Jet maker Embraer is also slated to post quarterly results late Friday. Its preferred shares lost 4.17 percent to 19.31 reais.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060512e25c001zz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
