\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil stocks,  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  stumble from record highs  \b0\par\par\uc2 431 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2006\par 16:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Brazil, May 11 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell nearly 2 percent on Thursday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars and investors fretted about a U.S. interest rate hike in June while stocks dropped further from an all-time high set earlier this week.  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> closed at 2.102 to the dollar, pressured by higher U.S. Treasury yields and bets \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep up aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the spot market to build foreign reserves and please exporters by weakening the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Still, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains near its strongest five-year intraday level of 2.053 per dollar, which was hit on Wednesday before the Fed raised interest rates by a quarter-percentage point and left the door open to more increases.  \par \par \uc2 The Sao Paulo Stock Exchange's Bovespa index <.BVSP> slid 2.17 percent to a preliminary close of 40,847 points. It set a record high on Tuesday after breaching the 42,000-point level for the first time.  \par \par \uc2 "Foreign investors are cutting positions, (U.S.) Treasuries yields pressured a lot and the market is a little stressed," said Julio Cesar Vogeler, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at the Didier Levy brokerage in Sao Paulo.  \par \par \uc2 Brazil's financial markets have soared to a series of record highs over the last year, helped by improving economic fundamentals and a high benchmark interest rate, currently at 15.75 percent, which foreign investors find attractive.  \par \par \uc2 But whenever the Fed raises interest rates, Brazilian returns lose a bit of luster.  \par \par \uc2 Local traders had been betting Federal hikes might end after Wednesday, when the Fed lifted its benchmark overnight federal funds rate to 5 percent. But their hopes were dashed by a post-meeting statement that suggested another increase might be necessary.  \par \par \uc2 Still, local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders say they expect heavy inflows after UBS said on Tuesday it would buy Brazilian investment bank Pactual for $2.5 billion, and Mexico's Telmex said it would boost holdings in long-distance phone carrier Embratel.  \par \par \uc2 At the stock market, beverages company Ambev , the Brazilian unit of InBev , fell 1.6 percent to 983 reais even though its first-quarter profit soared fourfold.  \par \par \uc2 Major telephone company Tele Norte Leste Participacoes fell 6.9 percent to 36.30 reais, after its parent company said it was distributing 3 billion reais in dividends and other payments to stockholders, and was planning a secondary share offering.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060511e25b0020g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
