\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's real hits 5-year high, stocks off record  \b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2006\par 16:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Brazil, April 27 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose to its strongest level in more than five years on Thursday on hopes for a pause in U.S. rate hikes, which normally lure capital away from emerging markets. Stocks retreated from a record set the previous session.  \par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real <BRBY>, firmed 0.61 percent to 2.106 to the dollar. It opened weaker but reversed direction after Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke said the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may take no action at one or more future meetings on official interest rates after a long series of increases.  \par \par \uc2 "More investments should arrive in the local market, as our interest rates are still attractive," said Jose Roberto Carreira, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the Novacao brokerage in Sao Paulo.  \par \par \uc2 A pause in U.S. rate hikes would give the real room to gain further on high domestic interest rates -- currently at 15.75 percent -- and record exports that have flooded the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with dollars.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent excessive real strength, but instead has only slowed the pace of appreciation. It bought dollars on the spot market on Thursday as part of an effort to build up foreign reserves. Exporters favor a weaker real.  \par \par \uc2 After closing above 40,000 for the first time on Wednesday, the the Bovespa <.BVSP> index of the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange slipped 1.44 percent to a preliminary close of 39,830 points.  \par \par \uc2 Interest rate hikes in China pressured local stock market sentiment because many Brazilian companies export to the Asian giant, which is moving to dampen growth.  \par \par \uc2 Telecommunications company Telemar , one of the heaviest-weighted stocks in the index, fell 1.19 percent to 37.25 reais after reporting a 25 percent drop in first-quarter profit.  \par \par \uc2 Local stocks hit record highs last week after Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  trimmed its benchmark interest rate to spur economic growth.  \par \par \uc2 More domestic rate cuts are expected, though on Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggested that additional cuts may be more limited than previous ones it made to boost economic growth.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|D|M|E|RBN|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060427e24r0023f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
