\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Brazil cenbank dlr purchases at $7.89 bln in 2006  \b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 17:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, official comments)  \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, Brazil, March 30 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $3.1 billion on the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the first 28 days of March, bringing the bank's total purchases this year to $7.89 billion, a bank official said on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The bank has been aggressively buying dollars on the market in recent months as it seeks to build up international reserves and, indirectly, weaken the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real <BRBY> continues to trade near a five-year high, irking exporters who say their products are becoming less competitive on global markets.  \par \par \uc2 As of Wednesday, Brazil had $59.84 billion in foreign reserves, up from $52.9 billion just over a year ago.  \par \par \uc2 Afonso Bevilaqua, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic policy director, also said the bank had bought back $1.37 billion in foreign debt so far in March, bringing the total amount of external debt it has retired this year to $4.2 billion.  \par \par \uc2 The buybacks are part of the government's plan to reduce its external debt load, which is now at its lowest level since 1995.  \par \par \uc2 Bevilaqua added that the Treasury had already contracted for $9.1 billion on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this year to pay back debt coming due this year.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Treasury have been working together over the last few years to build up foreign reserves, making the country more resistant to financial turbulence.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 BRAZIL\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060330e23u001fl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
