t22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt swaps to contain the rise of the real. Under the scheme, the institution took dollar-denominated debt and offered paper linked to local interest rates in return. This allowed foreign investors to take advantage of Brazil's towering local interest rates without bringing dollars into Brazil. However, the institution ceased these \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  two weeks days ago as, according to analysts, the bank had canceled out all its dollar-denominated debt and was uncomfortable about taking an active futures position in the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said there was little new in the comments of Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke after the market close Monday. His speech to the Economic Club of New York indicated U.S. fed funds would continue to rise but this would not greatly affect the liquidity in emerging markets, said one analyst.  \par \par \uc2 The market will be waiting for the release of February current account data later in the morning. Investors are divided over what figure will be announced, with estimates ranging from a deficit of $1 million to a surplus of $700 million according to a survey of analysts conducted by the local Estado news agency.  \par \par \uc2 Any figure at the lower end of this range would lead the real to weaken, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Investors are also waiting for the release of the U.S. producer price index later in the day. The index is expected to have declined in February due to lower energy costs.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Alastair Stewart, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511-3145-1479; brazil@dowjones.com \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 21-03-06 1328GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060321e23l000mm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
