\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Eases  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Rogerio Jelmayer and Tom Murphy  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 647 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 2006\par 18:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--A Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision to reduce the sales volume of so-called reverse swap contracts at daily auctions could be a signal that the bank wishes to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  less in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 The decision will almost certainly lead to a strengthening of the Brazilian real against the U.S. dollar, at least in the short term, analysts added.  \par \par \uc2 Thursday night, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced that it would offer the equivalent of only $200 million in the reverse swap contracts at Friday's auction. The bank had been offering the equivalent of $400 million per day in recent weeks.  \par \par \uc2 "The trend is toward a reduction of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market," said Joao Nunes, chief economist at Agora Senior, Brazil's largest stock brokerage. "This could even be the beginning of the end for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took a similar tack once before. From mid-November until early December, the bank was offering the equivalent of $600 million per day in the swap contracts. In early December, the bank suddenly downshifted to $400 million, causing initial losses to the dollar against the real but with quotations subsequently stabilizing.  \par \par \uc2 The reverse swap contracts offer investors the opportunity to exchange dollar-linked paper for bonds indexed to the Selic base rate. The attraction for investors is the high Selic rate of 17.25%. The auctions tend to support the dollar against the real by removing dollar-hedging instruments from the market.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began the auctions two months ago after the real hit a four-year high against the dollar of BRL2.169. The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped strengthen the dollar, with the real closing out 2005 at BRL2.325.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was welcome news to exporters, who complained that the appreciation of the real hurts their ability to remain competitive in overseas markets.  \par \par \uc2 Even with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's year-end \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real appreciated 14.2% against the dollar in 2005. A record 2005 foreign trade surplus of $44.76 billion strongly supported the real.  \par \par \uc2 Exporters say the full effect of the real's appreciation will only be felt in 2006. Indeed, the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey of market opinion, released Monday, shows a 2006 foreign trade surplus forecast of $38 billion.  \par \par \uc2 As for the real's near-term outlook, ABN-Amro Bank chief economist for Brazil Jakiel Santos said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement means "the bank is searching for a point of equilibrium for its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." He said the bank will try to find the right volume of daily swap contract sales to assure a trading range of about BRL2.25 to BRL2.30. In fact, that was the market range in trading Friday, although not without a significant dose of volatility. The real opened at BRL2.268 per dollar, up sharply from the Thursday close of BRL2.328. As of 1730 GMT, the real was trading at BRL2.280, after hitting a high of BRL2.267 and a low of BRL2.281. But Agora's Nunes said the real could drift higher next week if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintains the $200 million level for the daily swap auctions. He said the real could reach about BRL2.20 per dollar before stabilizing. "This kind of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a limit and could be close to ending now," said Jose Carlos de Faria, chief economist for Brazil at Deutsche Bank.  \par \par \uc2 The drumbeat of daily swap contract sales, supplemented by nearly daily cash dollar purchases at snap auctions, also goes against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's own 1999 decision to end its tight control of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and allow for a floating exchange rate.  \par \par \uc2 -By Rogerio Jelmayer and Tom Murphy, Dow Jones Newswires; (5511) 3145-1478; brazil@dowjones.com [ 20-01-06 1753GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060120e21k000w3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
