\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil stocks, real weaken before likely rate cut  \b0\par\par\uc2 450 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Januar 2006\par 15:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Brazil, Jan 18 (Reuters) - Brazil's stocks retreated on Wednesday for a second straight day after setting a record, while its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost ground on expectations of a sharper than usual interest rate cut and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar purchases.  \par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real <BRBY>, closed 0.5 percent weaker at 2.324 to the dollar in cautious trade on turnover of about $700 million, sharply lower than Tuesday's $2 billion, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar has been rising since yesterday on talk about the rate (cut) ... The push came mainly from futures due to price adjustments over Copom expectations," said the head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a big local brokerage.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Committee (Copom) will announce its rate decision later on Wednesday. It hopes to spur economic growth, which suffered last year, with an interest rate cut which would be its fifth since September.  \par \par \uc2 In a Reuters poll on Friday, 15 of 20 economists predicted a cut in the benchmark lending rate of 0.75 percentage point to 17.25 percent. Five said a half-point cut, as seen last month, was more likely.  \par \par \uc2 Lower domestic interest rates may diminish demand for reais among foreign investors. Some traders say rate cuts would blunt the real's gains more effectively than official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars for the 71st time since early October at a cut-off price of 2.232 reais per dollar and sold some $400 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts linked to short-term interest rates for the 38th time since November.  \par \par \uc2 The swaps cut demand for reais from foreign investors who seek exposure to \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lofty benchmark rate.  \par \par \uc2 Exporters favor both types of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because they have helped knock the real off a 4-1/2-year high, making Brazilian goods cheaper abroad. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it buys dollars to boost \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2 The Sao Paulo Stock Exchange's benchmark Bovespa index <.BVSP> fell 0.9 percent to 35,805, dropping below the recently-conquered 36,000 mark.  \par \par \uc2 The market's bellwether, state oil company Petrobras , dropped about 1 percent to 42.4 reais. Power company Light rose 2.4 percent to 15.65 reais per share after a newspaper report said its owner, Electricite de France, had hired Citibank to step up efforts to sell Light.  \par \par \uc2 Morgan Stanley on Tuesday recommended a defensive stance on Latin American stocks, suggesting prices may have neared a peak. Higher oil prices <CLc1> were also hurting local markets and driving up global risk, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060118e21i0016t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
