\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  ends 5-day gainer, stocks slip too  \b0\par\par\uc2 587 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2006\par 15:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds closing figures, writes through)  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Brazil, Jan 10 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended weaker against the dollar on Tuesday, the first time in six sessions after lackluster industrial data, while stocks fell for the second day after hitting a record high on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The real <BRBY> closed trade 0.53 percent weaker at 2.262 against the dollar on Tuesday after the government's IBGE statistic's agency said industrial activity rose an anemic 0.6 percent in November from the month earlier.  \par \par \uc2 The weak economic data raised expectations among economists that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would next Wednesday cut the benchmark interest rate, now at 18 percent, by a more aggressive 0.75 points to revive the flagging economy.  \par \par \uc2 "The indicator on industrial production early in the morning reversed the expectation of a fall (in the dollar)," Daniel Szikszay, the manager of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  desk at Schahin bank, said.  \par \par \uc2 Brazil's domestic interest rate, one of the world's highest, has attracted foreign investors seeking better returns and is a reason the real has rallied to its strongest in 4-1/2 years in recent months.  \par \par \uc2 The industrial output data overshadowed news that would normally help strengthen the real. Brazil's Treasury offered on Tuesday $1 billion in global bonds maturing in 2037 at 295 basis points over comparable U.S. Treasury notes, the lead managers Deutsche Bank and UBS said.  \par \par \uc2 The Treasury confirmed the yield at 7.557 percent with a coupon of 7.125 percent. The sale marks Brazil's first sovereign issue in 2006. The last time the government tapped global capital markets was on Nov. 29, when it sold $500 million in bonds due 2034.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exports competitive.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered to buy dollars on the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the 65th time since early October. The bank also sold 8,800 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts linked to short-term interest rates, canceling out about $416.5 million in debt instruments indexed to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The auction marked the 32nd time since November that the bank has offered such swaps, which have helped weaken the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The swaps allow investors to buy exposure to Brazil's benchmark interest rate of 18 percent without having to purchase reais. They also cancel out dollar-linked debt notes that were originally sold to prevent the real from weakening.  \par \par \uc2 The Sao Paulo Stock Exchange's benchmark Bovespa <.BVSP> index dropped 0.81 percent to 35.049 points as investors took profits for the second day after last week's rally. Wall Street was also down as the Dow Jones industrial average <.DJI> was off 0.19 percent in late trade.  \par \par \uc2 Bovespa turnover of 2.2 billion reais was above last year's daily average of 1.6 billion.  \par \par \uc2 The Bovespa hit three record highs last week after the U.S. Federal Reserve signaled that interest rate increases are nearly over, boosting investor appetite for high-yielding emerging markets like Brazil.  \par \par \uc2 The new market bellwether, state-run oil company Petrobras , finished up 0.17 percent at 40.91 reais.  \par \par \uc2 But telecommunications stock Telemar and steel company Usiminas were among the blue chips that posted expressive losses. Telemar fell 1.22 percent to 40.65 reais and Usiminas fell 1.87 percent to 52.60 reais.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|D|M|E|RBN|U|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060110e21a000ys\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
