\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Opens Weaker On Continued  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2006\par 13:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real opened weaker against the U.S. dollar Tuesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  looks set to continue its policy of buying dollars and dollar-linked debt.  \par \par \uc2 The real opened at BRL2.347 to the dollar, down from the Monday's close of BRL2.340.  \par \par \uc2 A change in \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules allowing banks to buy unlimited quantities of dollars on the spot market also will start to weigh on the market Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Late Friday, the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  ordered a rules change, abolishing previous limits on purchases of dollars on the spot market by banks. Previously, banks were limited to purchases of up to $6 million per day. As of Monday, banks faced no daily limits.  \par \par \uc2 The impact of the move was limited on Monday during light trade because of holidays in major financial centers such as New York and London, but the influence would increase Tuesday, they said.  \par \par \uc2 However, should the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduce the level of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to strengthen as investors continue to be attracted by Brazil's high domestic interest rates. Brazil's Selic base interest rate is a towering 18% per month.  \par \par \uc2 Market players see little indication that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will institute a sharp reduction in the base rate during 2006, despite political pressure to do so in this electoral year. A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey of analysts, released Monday, indicated a base rate of 15.94% for the end of the year, up slightly from the 15.92% forecast in last week's report.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it will auction approximately $400 million in reverse swap contracts Tuesday, the latest in a series of daily auctions. The auction offers investors the opportunity to swap dollar-indexed paper for bonds linked to domestic interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 Typically, the auctions favor the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because they remove a hedging mechanism from the market.  \par \par \uc2 On Monday, the bank sold swaps worth $412.5 million.  \par \par \uc2 -By Alastair Stewart, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511-3145-1479; brazil@dowjones.com [ 03-01-06 1204GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1156 1843  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060103e213000eb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
