\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real slips on  \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Januar 2006\par 15:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jan 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real slipped on Monday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market and after it scrapped a rule that discouraged brokerages from holding more than $6 million in their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  accounts.  \par \par \uc2 The decision to change the rule, made on Friday, seemed consistent with actions the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has taken since October to pull the real back from some of its strongest levels in 4 1/2 years in order to keep exports competitive.  \par \par \uc2 On Monday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars on the spot market to build up foreign reserves for the 59th time since October and sold \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps that cut demand for reais for the 26th time since November. Another sale of $440 million in swaps is slated for Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The real <BRBY> ended off 0.65 percent at 2.34 to the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "In principal, the market is thinking that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to see the real at a weaker level," said Miriam Tavares, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the AGK brokerage in Sao Paulo.  \par \par \uc2 Starting on Monday, brokerages were able to boost their holdings of dollars without penalty. Previously, brokerages were required to deposit dollar holdings in excess of $6 million at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and were not allowed to receive interest on them. The rule dated from a time when there was less faith in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The real gained as much as 20 percent against the U.S. dollar in 2005, thanks to inflows of dollars from record exports, better economic fundamentals and foreign investors who were anxious to buy exposure to Brazil's lofty benchmark interest rate of 18 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The real ended the year about 14 percent stronger after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened it.  \par \par \uc2 At the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange, the Bovespa <.BVSP> index gained 0.15 percent to 33,507 in thin volume.  \par \par \uc2 The index's new bellwether, state-run oil giant Petrobras , rose 3.76 percent to 38.09 reais. Weightings in the index are changed several times a year according to trailing trading volumes.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060102e212000ha\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
