\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Trading flat in holiday lull, outlook for 2006 solid  \b0\par\par\uc2 745 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 2005\par 11:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 29 (Reuters) - Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were firm on Thursday in lacklustre trade given the holiday period, but the outlook for a strong start to 2006 is set, say analysts.  \par \par \uc2  Price changes were driven by what few commercial transactions came through the market, as position taking was nil given books have closed on the year.  \par \par \uc2  "I think January is going to be a good month for emerging markets. Gradually during the autumn, it seems to have become more of a consensus view that the balance of risks and opportunities for emerging markets continues to be pretty good," said Mats Olausson, chief strategist for emerging markets at SEB Merchant Banking in Stockholm.  \par \par \uc2  Highlighting the tighter monetary policies from the U.S. Federal Reserve and of late the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Olausson said the global growth outlook is still likely going to provide opportunities from which emerging market economies can benefit.  \par \par \uc2  Thinly traded markets might show outsized reaction to U.S. economic data due later on Thursday, including weekly employment data at 1330 GMT, manufacturing data at 1500 GMT and existing home sales, also at 1500 GMT.  \par \par \uc2  "Politically of course all the elections in South America will have the potential to change some trends. Mexico, there is quite a high likelihood of a hung parliament and not much will actually change. Whereas the risks in Brazil are perhaps larger," he added.  \par \par \uc2  The major Latin American emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were little changed however Brazil's real traded slightly weaker on the interbank market at 2.343 per dollar <BRBY>. \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  57 times since October, buying dollars in an attempt to stem the real's strength while building reserves.  \par \par \uc2  Overall, central and eastern European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were slightly firmer.  \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty was up 0.13 percent on the day against the euro at 3.8560 <0#EURPLN=> while the Czech crown maintained a steady state just under an all-time high. It traded at 28.925, up 0.09 percent on the day <0#EURCZK=>.  \par \par \uc2  The Hungarian forint was unchanged at 252.01 versus the euro <0#EURHUF=>. The Slovak crown edged up 0.05 percent on the day against the euro to 37.83 <0#EURSKK=>.  \par \par \uc2  South Africa's rand fell 0.24 percent to 6.34 <0#ZAR=> versus the U.S. dollar, unable to gain from rising gold prices.     [20051229 105543 GMT]   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 LATEST    PREV   LOCAL    LOCAL  \par                                 CLOSE  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                        PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par                                                 IN 2005\par  EUROPE/MIDDLE EAST/AFRICA\par  Czech Rep.   <EURCZK=>   28.91     28.94   +0.09    +5.14\par  Poland       <EURPLN=>    3.85      3.86   +0.13    +5.89\par  Hungary      <EURHUF=>  252.01    252.00   -0.00    -2.73\par  Slovakia     <EURSKK=>   37.83     37.85   +0.05    +2.35\par  Romania      <EURRON=>    3.69      3.69   -0.04    +6.64\par  Ukraine      <UAH=>       5.04      5.05   +0.12    +5.21\par  South Africa <ZAR=>       6.34      6.32   -0.24   -11.00\par  Kenya        <KES=>      72.48     71.95   -0.73    +8.31\par  Israel       <ILS=>       4.58      4.59