\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real tumbles on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , stocks flat  \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 2005\par 15:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Dec 22 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell on Thursday after two days of gains as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the real, while stocks finished little changed after flirting with a record high earlier in the session.  \par \par \uc2 The real <BRBY> finished at 2.331 to the dollar, weakening 1 percent in thin trade, while the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange's benchmark Bovespa <.BVSP> index ended 0.01 percent lower at 33,512.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had strengthened the previous two days, rebounding slightly from nine straight sessions of losses. But it backtracked again on Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $399.5 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps linked to short-term interest rates and bought dollars on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 "On a day like today, with little volume, the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  end up having more of an impact," forcing the real lower, said one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Brazilian bank.  \par \par \uc2 The bank has been aggressively selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps and buying greenbacks in recent weeks, helping to knock the real off a 4-1/2-year high while also placating exporters who have complained that a strong local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is making their products less competitive on world markets.  \par \par \uc2 The so-called reverse swaps allow investors to buy exposure to Brazil's lofty benchmark interest rate of 18 percent without having to purchase reais. They also cancel out old dollar-linked debt sold to prevent the real from weakening.  \par \par \uc2 On Friday the bank will offer about $420 million in swaps. The bank has now sold swaps 20 times since November and bought dollars on the spot market 54 times since early October.  \par \par \uc2 In the stock market, bellwether Tele Norte Leste Participacoes, or Telemar , fell 1.37 percent to 42.41 reais, weighing on the Bovespa index.  \par \par \uc2 On the upside, state-run oil giant Petrobras rose 0.24 percent to 36.90 reais after it said it would pay about $140 million to buy gas stations from Royal Dutch Shell in Uruguay, Paraguay and Colombia.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|D|M|E|RBN|U|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051222e1cm001hz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
