\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Closes Weaker On Continued Govt  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 603 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2005\par 20:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real closed weaker Monday amid speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increase \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market.  \par \par \uc2 The real closed at BRL2.260 to the dollar, up from Friday's close of BRL2.253.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying dollars and dollar-debt nearly every day in recent months, but local banks are now speculating that the bank will resort to other measures to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid loud complaints from politicians and exporters that a real near four-and-a-half-year highs is hurting the economy.  \par \par \uc2 "There comes a point when \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  becomes a matter of honor," said Jose Julio Senna, director of the Sao Paulo-based MCM consultancy.  \par \par \uc2 Among the banks options are to allow exporters to delay the repatriation of dollars or to impose restrictions on real futures trading.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday, mopping up dollars on the spot market in the afternoon at BRL2.264 to the dollar and offering swaps of dollar-linked debt for interest rate-linked paper. The bank sold 7,600 contracts of the 12,500 contracts offered, or about $365 million worth of swaps, between 1400 GMT and 1500 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 Investors are on standby awaiting some key meetings this week. All eyes will be on the U.S. Federal Reserve on Tuesday amid speculation that the policy statement after the Federal Open Market Committee meeting may indicate an end to the series of interest rate hikes.  \par \par \uc2 Then on Wednesday, Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will decide whether to adjust local interest rates, which are some of the world's highest.  \par \par \uc2 Domestic banks say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may take a more aggressive stance on interest rate cuts when it meets Wednesday. The base Selic interest rate currently stands at current 18.5% per year.  \par \par \uc2 Market expectations are for a cut of 50 basis points, but one trader said that some banks had already priced in a 75-basis-point cut, resulting in some volatility in the market as domestic banks started buying January futures contracts and putting pressure on the spot market.  \par \par \uc2 News that local inflation appears to have cooled off in December fueled that speculation.  \par \par \uc2 Sao Paulo's Fipe research institute said its consumer price index rose 0.18% in the four week period to December 7 compared with an increase of 0.29% in November. The result came in below market forecasts, which pegged the rate between 0.23% and 0.36%.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Brazil's General Price Index, or IGP-M, was 0.06% higher in the first 10 days of December, a lower rate of acceleration than the 0.16% rise seen in the first 10 days of November. The result was in line with market expectations, which posted forecasts ranging from a drop of 0.03% to an increase of 0.21% for the period.  \par \par \uc2 Early indications that the Brazilian economy is bouncing back after a disappointing third quarter are offering support for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A number of firms have announced the cancellation of collective holidays over the Christmas period after seeing stocks fall over the last month.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Alastair Stewart, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511-3145-1479; brazil@dowjones.com \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Corrected Dec. 12, 2005 14:45 ET (19:45 GMT) [ 12-12-05 1912GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Brazilian real closed weaker Monday amid speculation that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will increase \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (In "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Real Closes Weaker On Continued Govt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " published at 2:12 p.m. EST, the direction of the real was misstated in the first paragraph.) [ 12-12-05 1944GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051212e1cc000wa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
