\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real stumbles on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , stocks fall  \b0\par\par\uc2 460 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 2005\par 16:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Dec 8 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell for the second straight day on Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acted to weaken the real, while stocks slipped further from a record high set on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The real <BRBY> lost 1.32 percent to end at 2.224 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sought to pull the real back from some of its strongest levels in 4-1/2 years by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in the market over the last two months, selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps linked to short-term interest rates and buying dollars on the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as it did on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has rallied about 20 percent this year, lifted by a steady flow of dollars into the market from booming exports and corporate bond sales overseas.  \par \par \uc2 It has also benefited from high domestic interest rates, which attract foreign investors seeking higher returns than those available in Europe and the United States. Brazil's benchmark lending rate stands at a lofty 18.5 percent.  \par \par \uc2 But the rally has worried exporters who fear their products could lose market share abroad.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has made it clear that it wants the dollar to rise (versus the real) and that's what the market is reacting to," said Alexandre Vasarhelyi, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at ING Bank in Sao Paulo.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $519.7 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, which allow investors to buy exposure to Brazil's base interest rate without having to purchase reais.  \par \par \uc2 The auction marked the 10th time since November that the bank has offered such swaps, which also cancel out old dollar-linked debt that was originally sold to prevent the real from weakening. On Friday it will offer an additional $625 million in swaps.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also bought dollars on the spot market for the 44th time since October.  \par \par \uc2 On the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange, the benchmark Bovespa <.BVSP> index fell 0.84 percent to end at 32,480, according to preliminary closing figures. Bellwether Tele Norte Leste Participacoes fell 1.43 percent to 41.45 reais.  \par \par \uc2 Still the index is near a record high hit this week. Low inflation and heavy demand among yield-hungry foreign investors have helped raise the Bovespa to records this year. On Tuesday it closed above the 33,000 points for the first time.  \par \par \uc2 The stock market has also gained of late on expectations the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will cut interest rates further to boost growth and revive the economy, which contracted in the third quarter from the second for the first time in two years.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051208e1c80016y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
