\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Brazil cenbank sells  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  swaps, real weakens  \b0\par\par\uc2 398 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2005\par 17:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, exchange rate, background)  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Brazil, Nov 18 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday sold 8,400 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts linked to short-term interest rates to replace $404 million in outstanding debt instruments indexed to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The auction marked the first time since March that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, which are designed to help prevent Brazil's hard-charging real <BRBY> from strengthening further against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The real, which opened sharply lower on Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced the auction, weakened further once the results were made public. In late afternoon trading, the real was 1.74 percent weaker than Thursday's close at 2.228 to the greenback, leaving it 20 percent stronger than where it started the year.  \par \par \uc2 The bank sold all contracts on offer at the auction, suggesting that demand for the swaps is strong. The swaps carried maturities between March 2006 and January 2008.  \par \par \uc2 The new swaps enable investors to buy exposure to Brazil's lofty benchmark interest rate without having to purchase reais and help diminish the impact of dollar-linked debt notes that were originally sold to prevent the real from weakening.  \par \par \uc2 The government heavily sold the dollar-linked debt in 2002 to prevent the real from weakening, later refinancing the bonds with \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps as they matured. Brokerage houses bought the paper to hedge against a potential depreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 These debt and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps are denominated in reais but pay investors at the current real-dollar exchange rate when they mature.  \par \par \uc2 The new swaps linked to short-term rates should help cut the riskiness of Brazil's big debt load by getting rid of dollar-linked debt at a faster pace, and allow foreign investment to keep pouring into the country without strengthening the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  too much.  \par \par \uc2 The real's rally has become a hot political issue of late, sparking an outcry from exporters who fear their products will become less competitive on world markets.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also tried to beat back the real's surge by buying dollars on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, though it says the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are aimed at building up hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 BRAZIL\b0 \highlight\uc2 -SWAPS (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051118e1bi002aj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
